<theme>
    <!-- Crystal v3.3 system view: 4:3 hero composition for the Nova (1280x960).
         - Baked 4:3 comic background with the blue info panel at
           x 0.013..0.28, y 0.17..0.97 (fractions of the 4:3 frame).
         - The 5 supplied heroes are rendered on their own, fullscreen.
         - Live text inside the panel: manufacturer badge, system name,
           description, game count, facts line.
         - v4.0.0: horizontal carousel of per-system hardware cards across
           the lower strip (y 0.70..1.00), much bigger cards, no clipping. -->
    <view name="system">
        <image name="sysBackground">
            <pos>0 0</pos>
            <size>1 1</size>
            <origin>0 0</origin>
            <path>./backgrounds/${system.name}.webp</path>
            <default>./backgrounds/_default.webp</default>
            <!-- v18.3.0: scheme tint (light=none, dark=darkened cool) -->
            <color>${sysBgTint}</color>
            <zIndex>1</zIndex>
        </image>

        <!-- v18.4.0: console hero logo. The commissioned per-system logo
             (art/console_logos/${system.name}.png) layered LARGE over the
             collage, which now reads as the background: the collage is
             darkened per scheme (sysBgTint) so the crisp logo is the
             undisputed hero. maxSize preserves each logo's native aspect
             (they range ~2.8:1 to ~5.3:1).
             v18.4.1: recentered. v18.4.0's pos x 0.485 sat the logo on the
             seam between the baked info panel (x 0.013..0.28) and the
             collage (confirmed on the user's Nova photo). The logo is now
             centered in the free region right of the panel: panel right
             edge 0.28 -> screen edge 1.0, center (0.28+1.0)/2 = 0.64.
             With maxSize 0.40 the logo spans x 0.44..0.84, clearing the
             panel by ~205px and the screen edge by ~205px. y 0.285
             unchanged: the tallest logo (0.40/2.8 = 0.143 high) spans y
             0.214..0.356, well above the carousel zone (0.640). z30 above
             the background, below all live text (z50).
             v18.4.2: bigger (maxSize 0.48 0.24, +20%), ~7 degree tilt and
             a small optical nudge (pos 0.64 0.30). The tilt matches the
             collage energy: the baked brush titles (gba, nds, ...) rise
             to the right (right side up). ES-DE rotation is in degrees,
             positive = visually clockwise (y-down screen space, same as
             CSS/canvas convention), so rotation -7 gives the right-side-up
             lean. rotationOrigin pinned at center (0.5 0.5) for a
             deterministic pivot. The user confirmed the lean direction on the
             Nova (xbox photo) and asked for MORE of everything: hero size,
             4x the angle, sitting lower.
             v18.4.3: maxSize 0.58 0.29 (the stage-limited maximum at 28 deg
             tilt; see bbox math below), rotation -28, pos 0.64 0.39 (the
             optical middle of the stage between the screen top and the
             carousel zone, lower than v18.4.2's 0.30). Tilted bbox math
             (28 deg; cos=0.8830, sin=0.4695) on the 4:3 frame: rendered
             width w is a fraction of screen WIDTH, rendered height h a
             fraction of screen HEIGHT, so h = w*(4/3)/aspect; rotated
             bbox W = w*cos + h*sin, H = w*sin*(4/3)... precisely:
             W_n = w*(cos + (4/3)*sin/a), H_n = w*(4/3)*(sin + cos/a).
             All logos are width-limited at 0.58 (min aspect 2.76 > 2.0, so
             w=0.58 for all). Measured VISIBLE-ink spans (alpha>0, PIL
             expand-rotate, centered at 0.64 0.39):
             - tallest gbc (2.760:1): ink x 0.392..0.885, y 0.110..0.633
             - user's xbox (3.185:1): ink x 0.410..0.888, y 0.112..0.673
             - widest psx (5.260:1):  ink x 0.376..0.898, y 0.179..0.630
             Left edge ~0.14 clear of the info panel (0.28); right edge
             inside the screen. KNOWN TRADE (accepted per the user's
             explicit HERO directive): the bottom spike tip of the
             taller logos (xbox/gba/gbc) reaches y ~0.63..0.68, dipping
             into the carousel element's transparent zone (0.640+) and
             tucking BEHIND the selected card's top edge (card z45 >
             logo z30, card top y=0.651) by ~0.02-0.03. The spike is a
             thin blue flourish; the tuck reads as intentional depth,
             stable across carousel positions (selected card is always
             centered). A literal 2x width (0.96) cannot fit the stage
             at 28 deg tilt, so 0.58 is the largest maxSize with real
             margins: 1.21x the linear width but ~2.5x the on-screen
             tilted footprint vs v18.4.2 (xbox ink area) plus 4x the
             angle - the HERO jump the user asked for, as close to 2x
             as the stage allows.
             y 0.285 -> 0.30 (v18.4.2) -> 0.39 recenters the larger logo
             The 5 systems with no logo asset (nes, psp, steam, windows,
             xbox360) resolve to a missing file and paint nothing - the
             same mechanism as the gamelist's missing-marquee case. No
             invented art. -->
        <image name="sysHeroLogo">
            <pos>0.64 0.39</pos>
            <maxSize>0.58 0.29</maxSize>
            <origin>0.5 0.5</origin>
            <rotation>-28</rotation>
            <rotationOrigin>0.5 0.5</rotationOrigin>
            <path>./art/console_logos/${system.name}.png</path>
            <zIndex>30</zIndex>
        </image>

