        <!-- 5. MARQUEE, the visual headline of the page: an INVISIBLE
             responsive region (24,44 424x252). Open whitespace - no mat,
             no frame, no blue rectangle, no fade. When the game HAS
             marquee art, the libMarquee image (z20) paints over this
             fallback completely: the fallback title sits at z19 with an
             opaque white background, LEFT-ALIGNED at the art's own left
             edge (x=24, the engine left-aligns maxSize art via origin
             0 0.5) and only 272px wide - the footprint of a 1:1 logo,
             so any art at least that wide covers text+backing and no
             ghost text shows through. When marquee art is MISSING, the
             image paints nothing and this element becomes the
             intentional mock masthead: the game title set in Anton
             (blocky display), left-aligned exactly where the art would
             sit, wrapping to two lines for long titles. ES-DE 3.4.1
             has no conditional visibility, so this deterministic
             layering is the mechanism. Residual edge: art NARROWER than
             272px (taller than 1:1) with a very long title can show a
             text tail beside the art - accepted, vanishingly rare for
             scraper wheel art. -->
        <text name="libMarqueeTitle">
            <pos>0.01875 0.1375</pos>
            <size>0.2125 0.0583333</size>
            <origin>0 0</origin>
            <metadata>name</metadata>
            <letterCase>uppercase</letterCase>
            <fontPath>./fonts/Anton-Regular.ttf</fontPath>
            <fontSize>0.0275</fontSize>
            <lineSpacing>1.0</lineSpacing>
            <color>${mockInk}</color>
            <backgroundColor>${mockBg}</backgroundColor>
            <horizontalAlignment>left</horizontalAlignment>
            <verticalAlignment>center</verticalAlignment>
            <zIndex>19</zIndex>
        </text>
        <!-- 5. MARQUEE, the visual headline of the page: an INVISIBLE
             responsive region (24,44 424x252). The real scraped marquee
             binds with maxSize (native aspect preserved, scaled as
             large as possible within the width, never stretched, never
             cropped) and is VERTICALLY CENTRED in the masthead zone
             (origin 0 0.5 at the zone centre y): wide logos get strong
             horizontal presence, tall logos use the full height without
             going tiny. No visible container around the marquee itself.
             The art paints over the z19 fallback title + its opaque
             white backing, so no ghost text shows behind real marquee
